   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Regular forms",
     "texto": [
      "In verbs in **-ar**, the **-a** changes to **-e**: **falar** → **fale** (speak), **fales** (you speak), **fale** (speak). In verbs in **-er** and **-ir**, the vowel changes to **-a**: **comer** → **coma** (eat), **partir** → **parta** (leave).",
      "In the plural, **-em** (**falem**, **comam**, **partam**) and **-emos** / **-amos** (**falemos**, **comamos**)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Irregular forms",
     "texto": [
      "**ser** → **seja** (be), **estar** → **esteja** (be), **ter** → **tenha** (have), **ir** → **vá** (go), **fazer** → **faça** (do), **dizer** → **diga** (say), **ver** → **veja** (see), **vir** → **venha** (come), **saber** → **saiba** (know), **poder** → **possa** (be able), **querer** → **queira** (want).",
      "You already know some of them from the formal imperative (chapter 17)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Espero que»",
     "texto": [
      "With **espero que** (I hope that) the subjunctive is used: **Espero que estejas bem** (I hope you're well). Watch out: the form is the one for **tu**: **estejas** (you), not **estás**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
